WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.200
67 Israeli lawmakers recommended Gadi Eisenkot to form the next government, outnumbering the 46 who backed Benjamin Netanyahu. This is Omni View, episode 228, a Turkish fund scandal detention, clashes driving people from Ethiopia into Kenya, and later how Israeli coalitions actually form. Israeli President Isaac Herzog, France 24 reports, will name on Sunday, November 8, the party leader who gets the first chance to assemble a government.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:35.100
After sitting down with the heads of every party in the 120-seat Knesset, Israel's Parliament,

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:40.640
seven lawmakers abstained from making any recommendation, and among the outlets the remaining

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:43.300
counts and the announcement timing are not in dispute.

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:48.460
What divides the coverage is whether those counts are ordinary coalition arithmetic after

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:52.800
systematic consultations, or a possible break from the current Prime Minister.

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:58.380
Netanyahu's extended period in office is the backdrop Al Jazeera uses for the same

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:03.480
consultations, and that outlet argues that recommendations flowing to opposition figure

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:08.940
Gadi Eisenkott open a real possibility of a leadership change even though Netanyahu's

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:10.960
party remains the single largest block.

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:16.840
Taken at full strength, the consultation account says Herzog did the work the presidency is

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:17.380
built for.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:22.620
He heard every party had in turn, and that the resulting tally is the decisive numerical

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:24.520
outcome meant to guide his choice.

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:29.720
This ordinary coalition arithmetic rather than a verdict on a long tenure, though even

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:33.880
that reading still has to concede that a name on a podium is not yet a coalition.

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:38.480
The tenure account says a larger share of the chamber can open the door to a leadership

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:43.280
change, even when the sitting prime minister's party is still the single largest block.

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:48.600
And that after an extended period in office, that distinction between largest party and

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:50.520
governing mandate is the whole point.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:55.360
Though even that reading still has to concede that the largest block has not vanished from

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:56.320
the bargaining table.

00:01:57.239 --> 00:02:01.979
An Istanbul court ordered former family minister and ruling justice and development party

00:02:01.979 --> 00:02:08.099
Deputy Chair Fatma Batul Sayankaya into custody on charges of violating Capitol Market's law

00:02:08.099 --> 00:02:13.779
and membership of a criminal organization, Reuters confirms, while her husband was released

00:02:13.779 --> 00:02:16.379
on the condition that he report regularly to police.

00:02:16.379 --> 00:02:22.199
The order sits inside a wider investigation into a multi-billion-lira investment fund scandal

00:02:22.199 --> 00:02:27.179
that hit the massavings of nearly half a million investors, led the financial regulator

00:02:27.179 --> 00:02:33.719
to dissolve 131 funds, and now takes in more than 430 people suspected of market manipulation

00:02:33.719 --> 00:02:37.519
and insider trading, 112 of whom have been arrested.

00:02:38.159 --> 00:02:44.279
Opposition Yeni Party Chairman Zaynil Emre says Cyan Kaya and her husband received 2.17

00:02:44.279 --> 00:02:50.899
billion lira after putting in 163 million lira and selling their shares shortly before suspected

00:02:50.899 --> 00:02:55.979
price manipulation triggered a market crisis. The couple denied wrongdoing, but transferred

00:02:55.979 --> 00:02:59.879
some of the disputed funds to an account designated by banking regulators.

00:03:00.539 --> 00:03:07.219
Main opposition leader Osgar Ozil, Deutscheweller reports, called for President Recep Tayyip Erdogan,

00:03:07.419 --> 00:03:12.459
either to resign or call early elections, saying senior government figures bear ultimate

00:03:12.459 --> 00:03:17.899
responsibility. Justice Minister Akun Gurlek has stated how many people have been detained,

00:03:18.479 --> 00:03:22.679
and that institutional account does not place legal responsibility on the president.

00:03:23.749 --> 00:03:30.109
Opposition leader Freeman M. Boway, BBC World News reports, was convicted by a Tanzanian court

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:34.629
of incitement after a trial that left him acquitted of the more serious charge of treason.

00:03:35.169 --> 00:03:38.989
The 58-year-old politician has been detained since April of last year,

00:03:38.989 --> 00:03:44.969
So this verdict is the close of a long stretch behind bars, as well as the close of the courtroom process.

00:03:45.449 --> 00:03:50.009
Coverage of the case has drawn attention to the treatment of political opposition in Tanzania,

00:03:50.469 --> 00:03:53.349
and that coverage does not assign the court a political motive.

00:03:54.297 --> 00:03:59.637
Southern Ethiopia has seen deadly clashes between armed groups that, France 24 reports,

00:04:00.017 --> 00:04:03.817
have driven tens of thousands of people across the border into neighboring Kenya.

00:04:03.817 --> 00:04:10.517
Ethiopia, Africa's second most populous country with around 130 million people, is experiencing

00:04:10.517 --> 00:04:16.377
multiple armed conflicts, particularly along borders between its regional states, the internal

00:04:16.377 --> 00:04:17.857
regions that make up the country.

00:04:18.357 --> 00:04:23.597
The people now in Kenya are one direct consequence of that internal fighting, which has intensified

00:04:23.597 --> 00:04:25.897
along those state boundaries in recent periods.

00:04:26.964 --> 00:04:32.384
Several Chinese firms that make only artificial intelligence chips, pureplay chip makers including

00:04:32.384 --> 00:04:38.644
more threads, meta-X and eluvitar core X, the South China Morning Post reports, recorded

00:04:38.644 --> 00:04:43.244
profits in the third quarter as they expanded production to meet demand created by United

00:04:43.244 --> 00:04:49.024
States export controls that restrict Nvidia's high-end processors from reaching the Chinese market.

00:04:49.524 --> 00:04:54.024
Those controls are rules that block certain high-end processors from being sold into China,

00:04:54.424 --> 00:04:58.004
and that restriction is what opened a gap local firms are trying to fill.

00:04:58.004 --> 00:05:03.444
Severe supply chain hurdles and soaring memory costs continue to cloud prospects for sustained

00:05:03.444 --> 00:05:08.564
long-term growth, so the quarterly turn does not in that reporting settle whether the gains

00:05:08.564 --> 00:05:09.084
will last.

00:05:10.265 --> 00:05:15.385
Eurozone retail sales purchases in the countries that share the Euro declined in September,

00:05:15.665 --> 00:05:20.105
the Wall Street Journal reports, as high energy prices continue to weigh on consumer

00:05:20.105 --> 00:05:21.345
confidence and spending.

00:05:21.965 --> 00:05:26.425
The monthly drop is part of a continuing pattern of subdued consumer activity linked

00:05:26.425 --> 00:05:28.185
to those elevated energy costs.

00:05:29.353 --> 00:05:31.973
United States sanctions on a Cambodia-based network

00:05:31.973 --> 00:05:33.353
are progress worth knowing.

00:05:33.813 --> 00:05:36.273
All Africa reports, because they target

00:05:36.273 --> 00:05:38.393
a transnational criminal organization

00:05:38.393 --> 00:05:41.453
accused of running international online scam operations.

00:05:42.173 --> 00:05:43.893
Hundreds of Kenyans who were rescued

00:05:43.893 --> 00:05:45.933
from scam centers in Southeast Asia

00:05:46.173 --> 00:05:49.033
have been identified as victims of the expanding networks.

00:05:49.713 --> 00:05:51.493
The sanctions are a response to the growth

00:05:51.493 --> 00:05:54.253
of forced labor scam centers, workplaces

00:05:54.253 --> 00:05:59.033
where people are made to run online fraud that have drawn victims from multiple countries,

00:05:59.233 --> 00:06:03.913
including Kenya, and the measures target the criminal networks responsible for the operations.

00:06:05.039 --> 00:06:10.659
Elsewhere, a Kenyan Court, BBC Africa reports, found Doomsday cult leader Paul Mackenzie

00:06:10.659 --> 00:06:17.459
guilty last month of murdering 191 people, all but one of them children. Battlefield tactics are

00:06:17.459 --> 00:06:23.419
shifting toward drones and artificial intelligence, CNBC reports, while the world's biggest defense

00:06:23.419 --> 00:06:27.139
firms continue to see strong demand for conventional military equipment.

00:06:27.899 --> 00:06:33.419
Karachi residents, France 24 reports, blocked roads and recent days over prolonged electricity

00:06:33.419 --> 00:06:38.879
outages and other daily hardships in Pakistan's largest city, a metropolis ranked near the

00:06:38.879 --> 00:06:44.655
bottom of global livability indices. To really understand how a government is assembled in Israel,

00:06:45.075 --> 00:06:49.235
you have to separate the election night seat count from a later recommendation process

00:06:49.235 --> 00:06:53.515
that can send the first mandate to a leader whose party did not finish first.

00:06:53.915 --> 00:06:58.895
The usual mix-up is to hear who won and assume that person automatically becomes prime minister,

00:06:59.415 --> 00:07:04.435
but proportional representation hands out seats according to each party's share of the national vote.

00:07:04.875 --> 00:07:09.175
So many parties enter parliament and no single one may hold a majority on its own.

00:07:09.875 --> 00:07:13.115
After the votes are counted, the president meets every party leader,

00:07:13.615 --> 00:07:16.415
asks whom they formally recommend to receive the mandate.

00:07:16.415 --> 00:07:21.195
state. The official first chance to form a coalition and tallies those recommendations.

00:07:21.815 --> 00:07:26.195
A simple majority of the recommendations is enough, even if no single party holds a

00:07:26.195 --> 00:07:30.995
majority of seats, which is why smaller parties and shifting alliances can determine the

00:07:30.995 --> 00:07:36.435
Prime Minister rather than the largest block alone, and why a coalition, an alliance of

00:07:36.435 --> 00:07:41.435
parties that can survive together in Parliament, often matters more than any one party's

00:07:41.435 --> 00:07:46.755
Ross seat total. That same process has previously allowed parties with fewer seats to assemble

00:07:46.755 --> 00:07:51.995
coalitions when they secured enough external support, so finishing first in seats does

00:07:51.995 --> 00:07:55.995
not by itself lock in the right to govern if the recommendations go elsewhere.

00:07:56.735 --> 00:08:01.555
When you next hear that someone won an Israeli election, check whether the report distinguishes

00:08:01.555 --> 00:08:05.975
the seat total from the recommendation count that actually decides who receives the mandate,

00:08:06.475 --> 00:08:11.095
and put two outlets from different regions side by side, so you can see which facts they

00:08:11.095 --> 00:08:13.155
share and where interpretation begins.

00:08:14.172 --> 00:08:19.432
France 24 and Al Jazeera both carry the Israeli recommendation numbers, and what differs

00:08:19.432 --> 00:08:20.112
is the frame.

00:08:20.952 --> 00:08:24.752
Systematic consultations as the guide for the president versus a possible leadership

00:08:24.752 --> 00:08:29.632
change after a long tenure, even with the current Prime Minister's party still the largest

00:08:29.632 --> 00:08:29.972
block.

